  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Primary path",
      "items": [
        "The browser POSTs /chat/stream and reads SSE: meta, status, citations, model, token, done.",
        "The route rate-limits, requires an LLM key, and rejects an unknown session before ChatService runs.",
        "ChatService stores the user turn, builds the prompt, streams tokens, then stores the assistant reply."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Context branches",
      "items": [
        "Greetings skip both branches. Otherwise retrieval runs only when that user has documents.",
        "Web search runs in research mode, or when the toggle is on and the query looks time-sensitive.",
        "Retrieval and search run together. Either one can fail and the answer still continues.",
        "A follow-up is rewritten first. A semantic cache can answer before either branch runs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust",
      "items": [
        "There is no login. The browser keeps userId in localStorage and sends it, defaulting to \"default\".",
        "CORS uses the configured allowlist. The token bucket key is the client IP plus that user id.",
        "Groq, Gemini, and Tavily keys stay in server settings and leave only on outbound HTTPS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "On the nodes",
      "items": [
        "Before the first token, the LLM call walks a fallback chain with a breaker and a quota guard.",
        "Local model ids are BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 and Xenova/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2.",
        "Google and Cohere appear in those same maps; this path draws the local ONNX backends.",
        "Chat history is chatbot.db. Chunk text is rag.sqlite3, with one FAISS file per user."
      ]
    }
  ]
